---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import Header from '../components/Header.astro';
import Footer from '../components/Footer.astro';
---

<Layout
  title="Terms of Use | ByteLite LLC"
  description="Terms of use for the ByteLite LLC website, covering founder reservations, the Founder Supporter Pack, product status and proprietary technology."
  keywords="ByteLite LLC terms of use"
  
>
  <Header slot="header" />

  <section class="legal-hero">
    <div class="container">
      <p class="eyebrow">Legal</p>
      <h1>Terms of Use</h1>
      <!--
        Moved to September 2026 for the live-chat section below. The privacy policy
        promises that material changes are dated; these terms should keep the same habit.
      -->
      <p class="legal-sub">Last updated: September 2026</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <div class="container legal-body">

      <div class="legal-section">
        <h2>This is primarily an informational website.</h2>
        <p>The ByteLite LLC website provides information about the company, its technology and its products. It is not a general consumer storefront. Two narrow commercial surfaces are planned - the founder reservation system described below, and the Founder Supporter Pack - and <strong>neither is currently able to take a payment.</strong> Their specific terms are still being drafted and are not published yet; they will be published, and you will be asked to accept them, before either can charge anything. No product is available for retail purchase through this website.</p>
      </div>

      <div class="legal-section">
        <h2>Commerce is switched off.</h2>
        <p>Payment on this website is handled by Stripe and is currently in <strong>test mode with every checkout control disabled at the server</strong>. A request to start a checkout is refused, not processed. No card is charged, no subscription is created and no payment method is stored.</p>
        <p>Where a product's price has not been set, this website offers a no-charge founder reservation rather than a paid preorder. Where a price exists but the product does not, it still offers a reservation. These terms will be updated, and you will be shown and asked to accept the change, before any live charge is possible.</p>
        <p><strong>Cordel Play</strong> is a physical product for adults aged 18 or over. It will not accept a paid preorder until ByteLite LLC has a reasonable basis for a stated shipment time and an operating delay-consent and refund process, as required by the FTC Mail, Internet, or Telephone Order Merchandise Rule.</p>
        <p><strong>The Founder Supporter Pack</strong> is a one-time purchase of digital goods from a for-profit company. It is not a charitable donation, is not tax deductible, and conveys no equity, repayment right, ownership, product access or control over development.</p>
      </div>

      <!--
        THE LIVE CHAT. Added 2026-09 alongside the /deep-kore page.

        Scope discipline: this section states only conditions the chat actually creates -
        what the conversation is for, what it is not, what a consent does, and the fact
        that ByteLite LLC may switch it off. It invents no warranty, no indemnity, no
        arbitration clause and no licence grant, because none of those is required by
        anything the feature does and speculative legal commitments are worse than none.
        The wording remains subject to owner and counsel approval.
      -->
      <div class="legal-section">
        <h2>The live chat.</h2>
        <p>This website offers a live conversational interface to Deep Kore, a ByteLite LLC system. It is provided for information and evaluation. <strong>It is not advice</strong> - not legal, financial, medical, technical or professional advice - and it is not a support channel: it cannot see your account, your order, your payments or your messages to ByteLite LLC, and it cannot act on your behalf. For anything that needs a person, use the contact form.</p>
        <p>Responses are produced by the system and passed through unchanged. ByteLite LLC does not warrant that any response is accurate, complete or fit for a particular purpose, and <strong>you should not rely on a response as a statement of fact about ByteLite LLC, its products, its pricing or its obligations.</strong> Where a response and the rest of this website disagree, the rest of this website governs; where this website and a signed agreement disagree, the agreement governs.</p>
        <p>When you use it, you agree not to submit secrets, credentials, payment details, regulated or health information, personal information about other people, or anything you do not have the authority to share. You also agree not to attempt to disrupt, overload, circumvent or reverse-engineer the system or the controls around it.</p>
        <p>The interface may be limited, suspended, changed or withdrawn at any time, and a session may be refused or ended - including when capacity is full, when the service is unavailable, or after a period of inactivity. Availability is not guaranteed and no session is guaranteed to persist.</p>
        <p><strong>Three decisions may be asked of you during a conversation, and each stands alone.</strong></p>
        <p><strong>Context.</strong> You may describe, in an optional panel, how you are related to a person or place you want to ask about. Every fact there is one you enter or select; nothing is derived from your messages. The name you use for someone is never transmitted. All of it is held in your browser only, and ordinary conversation works without any of it.</p>
        <p><strong>A private value.</strong> Where answering requires stating a specific fact back to you, you may be asked for that one fact by name. If you choose to send it, you authorise its use for <strong>that single answer only</strong>; it is discarded after that use and is not retained. Declining sends nothing. A permission covers one turn and is never a standing one, and sending a value once is not permission to send it again. Removing a value, or declining later, prevents any future use; it does not undo an answer that has already been given using a value you authorised at the time. Do not send a value you do not have the authority to share.</p>
        <p><strong>An unrecognised concept.</strong> Submitting one for review authorises <strong>storage of an unverified candidate only</strong>. It does not teach the system, does not add anything to what the system knows, and grants ByteLite LLC no rights in anything you submitted beyond retaining that candidate for review and deciding, separately, whether to act on it. Declining stores nothing.</p>
        <p>None of these is bundled with another, with any purchase, or with any other agreement.</p>
        <p>What happens to conversation content is described in the <a href="/privacy">privacy policy</a>.</p>
      </div>

      <div class="legal-section">
        <h2>Technical descriptions.</h2>
        <p>Descriptions of how ByteLite works on this website explain principles, objectives and claim boundaries. They do not disclose or license proprietary implementation, and they are informational rather than a representation of current product capability. Anything described as a target or an objective is exactly that, and must not be read as a claim of existing capability.</p>
      </div>

      <div class="legal-section">
        <h2>Founder preorder and reservations.</h2>
        <p>Where a product's launch price is not yet announced, this website may offer a no-charge founder reservation rather than a paid preorder. A reservation does not charge any payment method and does not obligate a future purchase. Separate preorder terms govern reservations and any future paid preorder, and are provided at the point of reservation.</p>
      </div>

      <div class="legal-section">
        <h2>Product status may change.</h2>
        <p>Product and project statuses described on this website reflect the best available information at the time of writing. No representation is made that any status is permanent or binding. ByteLite LLC may update, delay, cancel, or modify any product or project without prior notice.</p>
      </div>

      <div class="legal-section">
        <h2>Research claims are not production claims.</h2>
        <p>Research described on this website is private and ongoing. Research status does not constitute a claim of commercial readiness, public availability, or independent verification. No production infrastructure product is currently offered by ByteLite LLC.</p>
      </div>

      <div class="legal-section">
        <h2>Architecture descriptions.</h2>
        <p>Architecture and research descriptions on this website are informational and do not disclose or license proprietary technology. They explain the system design, research objectives, and claim boundaries; they do not constitute mechanism disclosure, patent claims, or production claims.</p>
      </div>

      <div class="legal-section">
        <h2>Proprietary technology.</h2>
        <p>ByteLite LLC's research methodology and technology systems are proprietary. Nothing on this website grants any license to use, copy, or build upon ByteLite LLC's systems. Use of any ByteLite technology requires a separate license agreement.</p>
      </div>

      <div class="legal-section">
        <h2>No warranties.</h2>
        <p>This website is provided as-is without warranty of any kind. ByteLite LLC makes no guarantee as to the accuracy, completeness, or timeliness of information provided. Use of this website is at your own risk.</p>
      </div>

      <div class="legal-section">
        <h2>Governing law.</h2>
        <p>These terms are governed by the laws of the State of Montana, USA, without regard to conflict-of-law principles.</p>
      </div>

      <div class="legal-section">
        <h2>Contact.</h2>
        <p>Legal inquiries may be directed through the <a href="/contact">contact page</a>.</p>
      </div>

    </div>
  </section>

  <Footer slot="footer" />
</Layout>

<style>

.legal-hero { padding: 5rem 0 3.5rem; }
.legal-hero h1 { max-width: 480px; }
.legal-sub { margin-top: .75rem; font-size: .9375rem; color: #555e7a; }
.legal-body { max-width: 760px; }
.legal-section { margin-bottom: 3rem; }
.legal-section h2 { font-size: 1.375rem; color: #e4e7f2; margin-bottom: 1rem; padding-bottom: .75rem; border-bottom: 1px solid #1a2235; }
.legal-section h3 { font-size: 1.0625rem; color: #e4e7f2; margin: 1.5rem 0 .5rem; }
.legal-section p { font-size: .9375rem; color: #7b829e; line-height: 1.75; margin-bottom: .875rem; }
.legal-section a { color: #818cf8; }
.legal-section a:hover { color: #a5b4fc; }
.legal-list { list-style: none; display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: .625rem; }
.legal-list li { font-size: .9375rem; color: #7b829e; padding-left: 1.25rem; position: relative; line-height: 1.6; }
.legal-list li::before { content: "—"; position: absolute; left: 0; color: #4a5068; }

</style>
